    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Ligurian port that became one of the great medieval sea powers, with colonies from Chios to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Caffa</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>.</li><li>It pioneered commercial contracts, marine insurance and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-saint-george">Bank of Saint George</a>, which managed debt, taxes and colonies.</li><li>After 1528 an aristocratic republic allied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, its bankers financed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> until c. 1627.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-saint-george">Bank of Saint George</a>, a creditors’ bank founded in 1407, governed the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a> on the republic’s behalf for over a century.</p></aside>
    </section>

